served as site/matrix/vendor-vlist.min.js

Why this one: it virtualizes a list without owning the markup, the framework or
the data. The estate's rooms are server-rendered HTML; a virtualizer that
insisted on rendering rows itself would have to become the renderer, and then
the room would exist twice. This one measures and positions what is already
there, which is the only part a browser is better at than the server.
